  "details": "With the addition of global physbone colliders, my first thought was things like tails colliding with people's body's and perhaps legs and such, for more interesting interactions between avatars, but of course, we can all imagine the jittery mess as physbones and colliders bounce off each other.\n\nSo my thought was if we had an adjustable \"compliance\" parameter for physbones and physbone colliders that reduced the elasticity of collisions. Something, a damping force applied to the force that pushes an object out of a collider when they overlap.\n\nThis could improve stability of soft body-to-body collisions, and help avoid twitching and glitching of physbones, and would potentially also provide a more natural look to collisions, in lieu of a volumetric soft-body simulation; allowing for some overlap between bodies that would otherwise be deforming in contact with each other.\n\nI have attached an extremely thorough visual aid of what I mean in regards to the last paragraph",
